  "status": "formal",
  "supportedClaim": "An outer lobe persistent for theta R^3 forces the exact Hölder lower bound with coefficient 2 sqrt(2). Two disjoint unit-dwell windows are realizable in one common-shear solution, but along the inherited adjacent-shell survival path theta=1 makes the normalized lobe-floor payment factor diverge. Bounded payment relative to that explicit witness therefore requires the displayed exponentially collapsing dwell ceiling."
}
